\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Real spin directions at a reflected site}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{On the product spin space in \ref{fdip-00LB}, let #{c}
conjugate coefficients in the real flip and sign basis.
It fixes each direction operator. Let #{\Gamma=Z^{\otimes n}},
where #{Z} fixes the first basis vector and negates the second.
Each direction flips exactly one factor, so #{\Gamma} anticommutes
with every direction. With a scalar fiber and ordinary conjugation,
the [spinor time map](fdip-017Z) sends the spin value at
#{\theta_s x} to its coordinate conjugate multiplied by
#{\Gamma\varepsilon_t}. Both operators in this product are real
self-adjoint involutions. They anticommute, so applying the
time map twice gives minus the original spin field.
The corresponding existence test for other direction operators
is the ordered trace condition in \ref{fdip-017K}.}
